  "repo_truth": "Review 3 independently admitted the exact 23-path subject and returned one Required durability finding: recovery did not explicitly replay the pending-directory fsync after observing a published committed or rolled-back marker and before terminal directory rename. The parent accepted it without waiver. This exact 24-path subject freezes that replay plus exact terminal-payload revalidation for W14, R8, both pending terminal predicates, the suffix partition, plan/checklist, and a symmetric two-marker-by-four-boundary fault product. Intent 1.2 and identity values remain unchanged; the verified dirty implementation snapshot is untouched; no Rust, immutable prior evidence, or HCM-2.3 surface changed.",
  "allowed_scope": ["Remain read-only and replay all 24 manifest hashes, lexical order, and aggregate before review.", "Independently review the complete identity/currentness/persistence/recovery subject, not only Review 3 or the fsync repair.", "Adversarially verify terminal-marker pending-directory-fsync replay, transaction/promotion identity separation, intent/output whole-file publication, 36 S-boundary plus eight terminal-marker fault pairs, absent-or-exact stages, W0-W15/R0-R9, collisions, mismatch evidence, and terminal parent-fsync replay.", "Return findings first with exact file/line evidence, failure mode, smallest repair, and missing validation."],
  "non_goals": ["No edits, staging, commits, handoff/ledger writes, snapshot mutation, or user task hops.", "No Rust/test work, implementation resumption, schema widening, fallback/dual read, relaxed validation, prior-evidence rewrite, HCM-2.3 work, or adjacent cleanup.", "Do not inherit prior verdicts; derive the whole result independently."],
  "tasks": ["Invoke the ordered required skills and return BLOCKED on any subject-manifest mismatch.", "Verify the complete identity graph, schemas/vectors, persistence, migration, currentness, writer/recovery, collision, mismatch, fsync, and fault-test grammar is exact and mutually consistent.", "Prove every published terminal marker under pending repeats child-directory fsync and payload validation before terminal rename, all journal paths use transaction_id, whole-file rules and fault products are complete, and scratch never enters recovery.", "Return CLEAN only with no Critical, Required, Optional, or Nit finding; otherwise return CHANGES_REQUIRED or BLOCKED without repair."],
  "contracts_and_gates": ["docs/specs/handbook-contract-membrane/slices/HCM-2.2/SPEC.md#promotion-transaction-intent-12-and-recovery", "docs/specs/handbook-contract-membrane/slices/HCM-2.2/contracts/promotion-transaction-intent-1.2.0.schema.json", "docs/specs/handbook-contract-membrane/slices/HCM-2.2/contracts/promotion-transaction-intent-vectors-v1.0.json", "docs/specs/handbook-contract-membrane/slices/HCM-2.2/proof/20260720T212648Z--atomic-stage-review-3-remediation-proof.md", "docs/specs/handbook-contract-membrane/06-proof-and-regression-ledger.md#hcm-22-constitutional-root-implementation-proof-gate"],
  "stop_conditions": ["Return BLOCKED if any subject path, hash, count, order, aggregate, authority ref, or reviewed-state prerequisite differs.", "Return CHANGES_REQUIRED if any identity/path, intent, scratch, verification, fsync, rename, recovery, mismatch, collision, currentness, migration, or fault-test rule is missing, ambiguous, contradictory, or broader than the repair.", "Do not waive/repair findings, create records, authorize/resume implementation, or begin HCM-2.3."],
